{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794789505,"nonce":"SNgSty6cWGtXtBWjGw9pbI9fOnw=","title":"rich_text_editor: stable block ids","message":"Low priority, not blocking anything. `Block` currently has no identifier, and the render path keys blocks by position (`key.index` in `content.rs`). A stable id per block (for example a short random or counter-based id, kept through insert, delete and move) would let apps refer to a block across edits: keep per-block widget state, restore focus or selection after a rebuild, attach comments, or sync a block with an external store.\n\nIds could be optional or generated on creation and kept on markdown import. Thank you for Blinc, and no rush on this.","files":null}]}